    "problem_statement": "Parser only reads first line of multi-line .env files\n\nDescription\n\nWhen parsing .env files with multiple lines, the parser only reads the first line and ignores subsequent lines. This affects both `dotenv_values()` and `load_dotenv()` functions.\n\nSteps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport io\nfrom dotenv import dotenv_values\n\n# Multi-line .env content\nenv_content = \"\"\"a=b\nc=d\"\"\"\n\n# Parse using StringIO\nresult = dotenv_values(stream=io.StringIO(env_content))\nprint(\"Expected: {'a': 'b', 'c': 'd'}\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {result}\")\n\n# Also fails with files containing multiple variables\nwith open('.env', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(\"DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost/db\\nSECRET_KEY=mysecret\")\n\nresult = dotenv_values('.env')\nprint(\"Expected: {'DATABASE_URL': 'postgres://localhost/db', 'SECRET_KEY': 'mysecret'}\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {result}\")\n```\n\nThe parser stops after reading the first key-value pair and doesn't continue to parse remaining lines in the file."
  }
